# PocketPilot Frontend

Mobile-first PWA for personal budget management. Single user, no auth, one active salary cycle.

Stack: React + Vite + Tailwind + Zustand. Backend: Node/Express/PostgreSQL (do not modify contracts).

## Hard Rules

- Navigation: React Router (`react-router-dom`) — routes in `App.jsx`, `BrowserRouter` in `main.jsx`
- Bottom nav routes: `/` (Home), `/income`, `/expenses` (Spend), `/transfers` (Rebalance), `/categories` (Budgets)
- Only Cycle Setup is gated (no active cycle). Other modules are normal nav pages
- `BottomNav` lives in `AppLayout` via `<Outlet />` — pages must never render it
- Always wrap pages in `ScreenLayout`; use `PageHeader`, `PrimaryButton`, `TextInput`
- Prefer existing components (`BalanceCard`, `BudgetCard`, `FloatingActionButton`) over new ones
- Avoid inline styles; use Tailwind
- Expect API envelope: `{ success, message, data }`
- Consume APIs exactly as documented in `docs/API_INTEGRATION.md` — do not invent or change contracts

## Theme (dark purple)

`#10002b` `#240046` `#3c096c` `#5a189a` `#7b2cbf` `#9d4edd` `#c77dff` `#e0aaff`

Rounded cards/buttons, minimal, dashboard-focused.

## Startup Flow

No active cycle → Cycle Setup (full screen).

Active cycle → Dashboard with BottomNav. Categories/Income are optional pages via nav.

## Stores

Exist: `cycleStore`, `categoryStore`, `incomeStore`, `expenseStore`, `categoryTransferStore`.

## Scope Split

Frontend owns: UI, Zustand, API clients, forms, validation, responsive design.

Backend owns: schema, SQL, routes, controllers, services, response shapes.

## Not Started

Reports, Settings, Analytics, Budget Alerts, Recurring Expenses.
